# Day 6/100 — Networking Fundamentals 🔐

Today I focused on strengthening my **networking fundamentals**, which are essential for understanding cybersecurity and penetration testing.

## 📚 What I Learned

### 1. OSI Model

* Studied the **7 layers of the OSI model**
* Understood the role of each layer
* Learned how data moves through the different layers

### 2. TCP/IP Model

* Studied the layers of the TCP/IP model
* Understood how it is used in real-world networking
* Compared the **OSI model vs TCP/IP model**

### 3. Common Networking Protocols

| Protocol      | Purpose                                |
| ------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| HTTP / HTTPS  | Web communication                      |
| FTP / FTPS    | File transfer                          |
| SMTP / SMTPS  | Sending emails                         |
| DNS           | Domain name resolution                 |
| DHCP          | Automatic IP configuration             |
| SSH           | Secure remote access                   |
| Telnet        | Remote access                          |
| POP3          | Receiving emails                       |
| IMAP          | Managing emails                        |
| NTP           | Time synchronization                   |
| SMB / NetBIOS | Windows file/resource sharing          |
| RDP           | Remote desktop                         |
| ARP           | IP-to-MAC address resolution           |
| TCP           | Reliable transport communication       |
| UDP           | Connectionless transport communication |

### 4. Database Services

I also studied commonly encountered database services:

* **Oracle Database**
* **MySQL**
* **PostgreSQL**

Understanding these services is important during network enumeration because exposed database services can become part of the attack surface.

